---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  noindex
  title="Contact — IncenseHub"
  description="How to reach IncenseHub for editorial corrections, sourcing questions, and privacy requests. This is a knowledge platform; there is no commercial inquiry process."
>
  <article class="article">
    <h1>Contact</h1>
    <p><em>Last updated: 2026-10-31 · Applies to this knowledge site</em></p>

    <p class="lead">
      IncenseHub is an independent knowledge platform for Chinese incense. This page lists the
      legitimate reasons to contact us — editorial corrections, sourcing questions, and privacy
      requests — and confirms plainly that there is no commercial inquiry process.
    </p>

    <h2>Why people contact us</h2>
    <p>
      Most messages fall into one of two groups:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Editorial — corrections and sourcing questions.</strong> If you spot an error, a
        mis-cited source, a broken link, or a claim you can correct from a primary source, tell us the
        page and the specific sentence. Corrections are handled through the process on our
        <a href="/blog/landeng-editorial-methodology/">editorial methodology</a> page.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Privacy and rights requests.</strong> Access, correction, or deletion requests under
        data-protection law, or questions about a legal page, are handled through the same address —
        see the <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a> for your rights.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Contact channel</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Email.</strong> <code>landengltd@gmail.com</code>. This is the single channel for
        editorial corrections and privacy requests.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="callout">
      <strong>Email:</strong> <code>landengltd@gmail.com</code>
    </div>

    <h2>Editorial corrections</h2>
    <p>
      To report an error, write with the subject "Correction" and tell us the page URL and the
      specific sentence. We correct errors at their source, update the page's review date, and — where
      a dataset is involved — log the change. We do not silently rewrite, and we do not delete retired
      entities.
    </p>
    <p>
      A note on what a correction is not: we do not revise content because it is unfavourable, and we
      do not remove a correctly sourced entry at a third party's request. A correction is a factual
      fix — an error, a mis-citation, or a genuinely outdated statement.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do not do</h2>
    <p>To set expectations plainly, we do not:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Take orders, prepare quotations, or run any commercial inquiry process — this is a knowledge platform, not a store.</li>
      <li>Accept unsolicited payments — there is no online ordering or checkout here.</li>
      <li>Respond to messages requesting medical advice — this site is informational and educational; see the <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a>.</li>
      <li>Publish customer case studies, testimonials, or "trusted by" logos.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="faq">Frequently asked questions</h2>
    <h3>Is this site a store?</h3>
    <p>
      No. There is no online ordering, payment, checkout, or quote process. IncenseHub is a knowledge
      platform that documents Chinese incense — materials, history, terminology, and craft.
    </p>
    <h3>How do I report an error?</h3>
    <p>
      Email <code>landengltd@gmail.com</code> with the subject "Correction", the page URL, and the
      specific sentence.
    </p>

    <h2>Related pages</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a> ·
      <a href="/terms-of-service/">Terms of Service</a> ·
      <a href="/cookies/">Cookie Policy</a> ·
      <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> ·
      <a href="/safety/">Safety</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
